\begin{abstract}
Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models have advanced robot manipulation toward general-purpose deployment, yet collision safety remains an open practical challenge for real-world use. Most existing safety methods operate at inference time, adding computational overhead; training-time alternatives based on reinforcement learning reduce violations but lack geometric grounding for precise spatial collision reasoning.

